
==========================
 * From theorem premises:
A B C D E F : Points
∠CBA = ∠ACB [00]
C,A,D are collinear [01]
BD ⟂ AC [02]
B,A,E are collinear [03]
CE ⟂ AB [04]
B,F,D are collinear [05]
C,E,F are collinear [06]

 * Auxiliary Constructions:
: Points


 * Proof steps:
001. C,A,D are collinear [01] & B,A,E are collinear [03] & CE ⟂ AB [04] & BD ⟂ AC [02] ⇒  ∠CDB = ∠CEB [07]
002. B,A,E are collinear [03] & C,A,D are collinear [01] & ∠CBA = ∠ACB [00] ⇒  ∠CBE = ∠DCB [08]
003. ∠CDB = ∠CEB [07] & ∠CBE = ∠DCB [08] (Similar Triangles)⇒  CE = BD [09]
004. ∠CDB = ∠CEB [07] & ∠CBE = ∠DCB [08] (Similar Triangles)⇒  BE = CD [10]
005. CE = BD [09] ⇒  CE:CD = CE:CD [11]
006. C,A,D are collinear [01] & B,F,D are collinear [05] & C,E,F are collinear [06] & B,A,E are collinear [03] & CE ⟂ AB [04] & BD ⟂ AC [02] ⇒  ∠CDF = ∠FEB [12]
007. C,F,E are collinear [06] & B,F,D are collinear [05] ⇒  ∠CFD = ∠EFB [13]
008. ∠CDF = ∠FEB [12] & ∠CFD = ∠EFB [13] (Similar Triangles)⇒  CF:CD = BF:BE [14]
009. BF:BE = CF:CD [14] & CD = BE [10] ⇒  BF:CD = CF:CD [15]
010. CE:CD = CE:CD [11] & BF:CD = CF:CD [15] ⇒  CF = BF
==========================
